  FT["PH-H3202"] = {"id":"PH-H3202","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3899_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"修订第1928号共和国法，规定马尼拉市官员薪酬的法案","en":"An Act Amending Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Twenty-Eight By Fix­ing the Compensation of the Officials of the City of Manila","orig":"An Act Amending Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Twenty-Eight By Fix­ing the Compensation of the Officials of the City of Manila"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["general"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3899","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3899_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3202-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"Section one of Republic Act Numbered Nineteen hundred and twentyeight is amended to read as follows:\n\"Section 1. The provisions of the Revised Charter of the City of Manila, as amended, to the contrary notwithstanding, officials of the city shall receive the following annual compensation:\nMayor ₱20,000.00 Vice-Mayor 18,000.00 Secretary to the Mayor 16,000.00 Secretary to the Board 14,000.00 Two assistant Secretaries to the Mayor, each at ₱14,000.00 28,000.00 Twenty Councilors, each at ₱14,000.00 280,000.00 City Engineer 16,000.00 Assistant City Engineer 14,000.00 Chief of Police 16,000.00 Deputy Chief of Police 14,000.00 Chief, Detective Bureau 14,000.00 Chief, Fire Department 16,000.00 Deputy Chief, Fire Department 14,000.00 City Treasurer 16,000.00 Assistant City Treasurer 14,000.00 City Assessor 16,000.00 Assistant City Assessor 14,000.00 Assistant City Health Officer 14,000.00 City Health Officer 16,000.00 Superintendent of City Schools including the National share of ₱7,200 per annum 16,000.00 Two Assistant Superintendent of City Schools, each at ₱14,000.00 28,000.00 City Auditor 16,000.00 Assistant City Auditor 14,000.00 City Public Service Officer 16,000.00 Assistant City Public Service Officer 14,000.00"}},{"id":"PH-H3202-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The incumbent officials holding the positions affected by this Act shall receive the salary increases upon the effectivity thereof without the necessity of a new appointment."}},{"id":"PH-H3202-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved, June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Amending Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Twenty-Eight By Fix­ing the Compensation of the Officials of the City of Manila","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3203"] = {"id":"PH-H3203","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3900_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将卡坦端内斯省的Catanduanes中等学校改设为国立中学并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act to Convert the Catanduanes Secondary School in the Province of Catanduanes into a National High School and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act to Convert the Catanduanes Secondary School in the Province of Catanduanes into a National High School and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3900","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3900_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3203-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The present Catanduanes Secondary School in the Province of Catanduanes is hereby converted into a national high school."}},{"id":"PH-H3203-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Secretary of Education shall reorganize the said school accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H3203-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The sum of two hundred thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the conversion, operation and maintenance of said school during the fiscal year nineteen hundred and sixty-five. Thereafter, such sums as may be necessary for its operation and maintenance shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3203-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act to Convert the Catanduanes Secondary School in the Province of Catanduanes into a National High School and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3204"] = {"id":"PH-H3204","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3901_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"在邦板牙省Floridablanca市镇设立国立农业学校，名称为Floridablanca国立农业学校，并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act to Establish a National Agricultural School in the Municipality of Floridablanca, Province of Pampanga, to be Known as Floridablanca National Agricultural School, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act to Establish a National Agricultural School in the Municipality of Floridablanca, Province of Pampanga, to be Known as Floridablanca National Agricultural School, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education","environment"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3901","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3901_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3204-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There shall be established, under the direct supervision of the Director of Vocational Education, a national agricultural school in the Municipality of Floridablanca, Province of Pampanga, to be known as Floridablanca National Agricultural School: Provided, That a suitable site of at least one hundred hectares of contiguous rich agricultural land shall be acquired."}},{"id":"PH-H3204-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"Upon the recommendation of the Director of Vocational Education, the President of the Philippines shall set aside and reserve such portion of the public lands located within the Municipality of Floridablanca, Province of Pampanga, as may be necessary and convenient for the establishment of the school and farm sites."}},{"id":"PH-H3204-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The sum of three hundred thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the establishment, operation and maintenance of said school for the first year. Thereafter, the necessary sum for said purpose shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3204-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act to Establish a National Agricultural School in the Municipality of Floridablanca, Province of Pampanga, to be Known as Floridablanca National Agricultural School, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3205"] = {"id":"PH-H3205","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3902_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":16,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授予 Audience Incorporated 在菲律宾境内建设、维护和运营无线电广播与电视站的特许经营权法案","en":"An Act Granting the Audience Incorporated, a Franchise to Construct, Maintain and Operate Radio Broadcasting and Television Stations Within the Philippines","orig":"An Act Granting the Audience Incorporated, a Franchise to Construct, Maintain and Operate Radio Broadcasting and Television Stations Within the Philippines"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["investment","company"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3902","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 16 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3902_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3205-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"Subject to the provision of the Constitution, the Audience Incorporated, is hereby granted a franchise for twenty-five years to construct, maintain and operate, for commercial purposes and in the public interest, radio broadcasting and television stations within the Philippines: Provided, That this franchise shall be void unless the construction of at least one television station or one radio broadcasting station be begun within four years from the date of approval of this Act, and be completed within five years from said date: Provided, further, That the grantee shall provide adequate public service time to enable the Government, through the said television and radio broadcasting stations, to reach the population on important public issues; shall assist in the functions of public information and education; shall conform to the ethics of honest enterprises; and shall not use its stations for the broadcasting and/or telecasting of obscene or indecent language, speech, act or scene, or for the dissemination of deliberately false information or wilful misrepresentation, or to the detriment of the public health, or to incite, encourage, or assist in subversive or treasonable acts."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"Such provisions of Act Numbered Thirty-eight hundred forty-six, entitled \"An Act providing for the regulation of radio stations and radio communications in the Philippine Islands, and for other purposes;\" Act Numbered Thirty-nine hundred ninety-seven, known as the Radio Broadcasting Law; Commonwealth Act Numbered One hundred forty-six, known as the Public Service Act, and their amendments, as are applicable to radio broadcasting stations shall be applied, as far as practicable, to the television stations referred to in Section one hereof."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"As a condition of the granting of this franchise, the grantee shall execute a bond in favor of the Government of the Philippines, in the sum of fifty thousand pesos, in form and with sureties satisfactory to the Secretary of Public Works and Communications, conditioned upon the faithful performance of the grantee’s obligations hereunder during the first three years of the life of this franchise. If, after four years from the date of acceptance of this franchise, the grantee shall have fulfilled said obligations, or as soon thereafter as the grantees shall have fulfilled the same, the bond aforesaid shall be cancelled by the Secretary of Public Works and Communications."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"Acceptance of this franchise shall be given in writing within six months after the approval of this Act. When so accepted by the grantee and upon approval of the bond aforesaid by the Secretary of Public Works and Communications the grantee shall be empowered to exercise the privilege granted thereby."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"The grantee’s radio broadcasting and television stations shall not be put in actual operation until the Secretary of Public Works and Communications shall have allotted to the grantee the frequency and wave lengths to be used under this franchise and issued to the grantee a license for such use."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"In the event of any competing individual, partnership or corporation receiving from the Congress a similar franchise in which there shall be any term or terms more favorable than those herein granted or tending to place the herein grantee at any disadvantage, then such term or terms shall ipso facto become a part of the grantee as in the case of said competing individual, partnership or corporation."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"(a) The grantee shall be liable to pay the same taxes on its real estate, buildings and personal property, exclusive of this franchise, as other persons or corporations are now or hereafter may be required by law to pay.\n(b) The grantee shall further be liable to pay all other taxes that may be imposed by the National Internal Revenue Code by reason of this franchise."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall hold the national, provincial and municipal governments of the Philippines harmless from all claims, accounts, demands, or actions arising out of accident or injuries, whether to property or to persons, caused by the construction or operation of the stations of the grantee."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"The franchise hereby granted shall be subject to amendment, alteration, or repeal by the Congress of the Philippines when the public interest so requires."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"In the event the Government should desire to maintain and operate for itself any or all of the stations herein authorized, the grantee shall turn over such station or stations to the Government with all the serviceable equipment therein at cost, less reasonable depreciation."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"A special right is reserved to the President of the Philippines in time of war, rebellion, public peril, emergency, calamity, disaster or disturbance of peace and order, to cause the closing of said stations or to authorize the temporary use and operation thereof by any department of the Government upon due compensation to the grantee for the use of said stations during the period when they shall be so operated."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall not require any previous censorship of any speech, play, act or scene or other matter to be broadcast and/or telecast from its stations; but if any such speech, play, act or scene or other matter should constitute a violation of the law or infringement of a private right, the grantee shall be free from any liability, civil or criminal, for such speech, play, act or scene or other matter: Provided, That the grantee, during any broadcast and/or telecast, shall cut off from the air the speech, play, act or scene or other matter being broadcast and/or telecast, if the tendency thereof is to propose and/or incite treason, rebellion or sedition, or the language used therein or the theme thereof is indecent or immoral, and wilful failure to do so shall constitute a valid cause for the cancellation of this franchise."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall not lease, transfer, grant the usufruct of, sell or assign this franchise or the right and privileges acquired thereunder to any person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity, nor merge with any other company or corporation organized for the same purpose, without the previous approval of the Congress of the Philippines. Any corporation to which this franchise is sold, transferred or assigned, shall be subject to all the conditions, terms, restrictions and limitations of this franchise as fully and completely and to the same extent as if the franchise had been originally granted to the said person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"text":{"en":"Wherever in this franchise the term \"grantee\" is used: it shall be held and understood to mean the Audience Incorporated, its representatives, successors or assigns, unless the context indicates otherwise."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"text":{"en":"This franchise shall not be interpreted as an exclusive grant of the privileges herein provided for."}},{"id":"PH-H3205-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Granting the Audience Incorporated, a Franchise to Construct, Maintain and Operate Radio Broadcasting and Television Stations Within the Philippines","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3206"] = {"id":"PH-H3206","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3903_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"规定在伊洛伊洛省Passi市镇建设或设立区域医院，名称为Passi区域医院，并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act to Provide for the Construction or Establishment of a Regional Hospital in the Municipality of Passi, Province of Iloilo, to be Known as Passi Regional Hospital, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act to Provide for the Construction or Establishment of a Regional Hospital in the Municipality of Passi, Province of Iloilo, to be Known as Passi Regional Hospital, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["health"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3903","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3903_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3206-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There shall be established, under the direct supervision of the Director of Medical Services, a hospital in the Municipality of Passi, Province of Iloilo, to be known as Passi Regional Hospital."}},{"id":"PH-H3206-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The sum of four hundred thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated, out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the establishment, operation and maintenance of said hospital during the fiscal year nineteen hundred sixty-five. Thereafter, such sums as may be needed for its operation and maintenance shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3206-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act to Provide for the Construction or Establishment of a Regional Hospital in the Municipality of Passi, Province of Iloilo, to be Known as Passi Regional Hospital, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3207"] = {"id":"PH-H3207","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3904_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":14,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授予 San Jose Cement Corporation 在菲律宾境内建设、设立、维护和运营私人固定点对点、海岸与陆基无线电台的临时许可的法案","en":"An Act Granting the San Jose Cement Corporation a Temporary Permit to Construct, Establish, Maintain and Operate Private Fixed Point-to-Point, Private Coastal and Private Land-Based Radio Stations for the Reception and Transmission of Radio Communications Within the Philippines","orig":"An Act Granting the San Jose Cement Corporation a Temporary Permit to Construct, Establish, Maintain and Operate Private Fixed Point-to-Point, Private Coastal and Private Land-Based Radio Stations for the Reception and Transmission of Radio Communications Within the Philippines"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["general"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3904","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 14 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3904_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3207-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There is hereby granted to the San Jose Cement Corporation a temporary permit to construct, establish, maintain and operate in the Philippines, at such places as the grantee may select, subject to the approval of the Secretary of Public Works and Communications, private fixed point-to-point, private coastal and private land-based radio stations, for the reception and transmission of wireless messages on radiotelegraphy or radiotelephony, each station to be provided with a radio transmitting apparatus and radio receiving apparatus."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The President of the Philippines shall have the power and authority to permit the location of said private fixed point-to-point, private coastal and private land-based radio stations or any of them on lands of the public domain upon such terms as he may prescribe."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This temporary permit shall continue to be in force during the time that the Government has not established similar service at the places selected by the grantee, and is granted upon the express condition that the same shall be void unless the construction of at least one of the stations be begun within one and one-half years from the date of the approval of this Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, shall not engage in domestic business of telecommunications in the Philippines without further special assent of the Congress of the Philippines, it being understood that the purpose of this temporary permit is to secure to the grantee the right to construct, establish, maintain and operate private fixed point-to-point, private coastal and private land-based radio stations, at such places in the Philippines as the interest of the corporation and of its business may justify."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"No fees are chargeable, as the radio stations that may be established by virtue of this Act shall engage in communications regarding the grantee’s business only."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, shall so construct and operate its radio stations as not to interfere with the operation of other radio stations maintained and operated in the Philippines."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, is authorized to operate its private fixed point-to-point, private coastal and private land-based stations in the medium frequency, high frequency, and very high frequency that may be assigned to it by the Secretary of Public Works and Communications."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, shall hold the national, provincial and municipal governments of the Philippines harmless from all claims, accounts, demands, or actions arising out of accidents or injuries, whether to property or to persons, caused by the construction or operation of its radio stations."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, shall be subject to the corporation laws of the Philippines now existing or hereafter enacted."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, shall not lease, transfer, grant the usufruct of sell or assign this temporary permit, or the rights or privileges acquired thereunder to any person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity, nor merge with any other persons, firm, company, or corporation organized for the same purpose, without the approval of the Congress of the Philippines first had. Any corporation to which this temporary permit may be sold, transferred or assigned, shall be subject to the corporation laws of the Philippines now existing or hereafter enacted, and any person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity to which this temporary permit is sold, transferred, or assigned shall be subject to all conditions, terms, restrictions and limitations of this temporary permit as fully and completely and to the same extent as if the temporary permit had been originally granted to the said person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"A special right is hereby reserved to the President of the Philippines in time of war, insurrection, public peril, emergency, calamity or disaster to cause the closing of the grantee’s radio stations or to authorize the temporary use and possession thereof by any department of the Government upon payment of just compensation."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"Wherever in this permit the term \"grantee\" is used, it shall be held and understood to mean \"San Jose Cement Corporation,\" its representatives, successors or assigns, unless the context indicates otherwise."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"This temporary permit shall be subject to amendment, alteration, or repeal by the Congress of the Philippines when the public interest so requires, and shall not be interpreted as an exclusive grant of the privileges herein provided for."}},{"id":"PH-H3207-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Granting the San Jose Cement Corporation a Temporary Permit to Construct, Establish, Maintain and Operate Private Fixed Point-to-Point, Private Coastal and Private Land-Based Radio Stations for the Reception and Transmission of Radio Communications Within the Philippines","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3208"] = {"id":"PH-H3208","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3905_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"规定在西米萨米斯省Baliangao市镇设立渔业学校，名称为Baliangao渔业学校，并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of a School of Fisheries in the Municipality of Baliangao, Province of Misamis Occidental, to be Known as the Baliangao School of Fisheries and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of a School of Fisheries in the Municipality of Baliangao, Province of Misamis Occidental, to be Known as the Baliangao School of Fisheries and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["environment","education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3905","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3905_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3208-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There shall be established under the supervision of the Director of Vocational Education, a school of fisheries in the Municipality of Baliangao, Province of Misamis Occidental, to be known as the Baliangao School of Fisheries."}},{"id":"PH-H3208-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The sum of one hundred thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the establishment, operation and maintenance of said school during the fiscal year nineteen hundred sixty-five. Thereafter, such sum as may be needed for its operation and maintenance shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3208-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of a School of Fisheries in the Municipality of Baliangao, Province of Misamis Occidental, to be Known as the Baliangao School of Fisheries and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3209"] = {"id":"PH-H3209","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3906_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"在邦板牙省Bacolor的San Vicente设立菲律宾工匠试点学校，名称为中央吕宋菲律宾工匠试点学校，并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act to Establish a Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen at San Vicente, Bacolor, Pampanga, to be Known as Central Luzon Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act to Establish a Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen at San Vicente, Bacolor, Pampanga, to be Known as Central Luzon Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3906","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3906_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3209-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There is hereby established a pilot school for Philippine craftsmen at San Vicente, Bacolor, Pampanga, to be known as Central Luzon Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen."}},{"id":"PH-H3209-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Secretary of Education, who shall exercise administration and supervision over said school, is authorized to issue such rules and regulations as may be necessary to carry out the purpose of this Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3209-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The sum of five hundred fifty thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the establishment, operation and maintenance of said school during the fiscal year nineteen hundred sixty-five. Thereafter, such sums as may be needed for its operation and maintenance shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3209-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act to Establish a Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen at San Vicente, Bacolor, Pampanga, to be Known as Central Luzon Pilot School for Philippine Craftsmen, and to Authorize the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3210"] = {"id":"PH-H3210","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3907_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授予 Pioneer 电力与制冰公司在南三宝颜省 Pagadian 市镇安装、运营电灯、热力与动力系统及制冰厂服务的特许权","en":"An Act Granting the Pioneer Electric and Ice Plant, Inc. a Franchise to Install, Operate and Maintain an Electric Light, Heat and Power System, and Ice Plant Service in the Municipality of Pagadian, Province of Zamboanga del Sur","orig":"An Act Granting the Pioneer Electric and Ice Plant, Inc. a Franchise to Install, Operate and Maintain an Electric Light, Heat and Power System, and Ice Plant Service in the Municipality of Pagadian, Province of Zamboanga del Sur"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["investment"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3907","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3907_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3210-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"Subject to the provisions of the Constitution and to the terms and conditions established in Act Numbered Thirty-six hundred and thirty-six, as amended by Commonwealth Act Numbered One hundred and thirty-two, there is granted to the Pioneer Electric and Ice Plant, Inc., for a period of fifty years from the approval of this Act, the right, privilege and authority to construct, operate and maintain an electric light, heat and power system and an ice plant for the purpose of generating and distributing electric light, heat and/or power, and manufacturing ice for sale within the Municipality of Pagadian, Province of Zamboanga del Sur. The grantee shall further have the right and privilege to install, lay and maintain on all streets, public thoroughfares, bridges and public places within said limits, poles, wires, transformers, capacitors, overhead protective devices, and pole line hardware, and other equipment necessary for the safe distribution of electric current to the public."}},{"id":"PH-H3210-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"In the event that the grantee shall purchase and secure from the National Power Corporation electric heat and power, the National Power Corporation is hereby authorized to negotiate and transact business for the benefit and in behalf of the public consumers with reference to rates subject to the approval of the Public Service Commission."}},{"id":"PH-H3210-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"In consideration of the franchise and rights hereby granted, the grantee shall pay into the Treasury of the Philippines a franchise tax equal to two per centum of the gross earnings for electric current sold under this franchise in lieu of all other taxes, fees and assessments of whatever authority upon privileges, earnings, income, franchise, and transformers, meters and generators of the grantee, from which taxes, fees and assessments the grantee is hereby exempted."}},{"id":"PH-H3210-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"It is expressly provided that in the event the Government should desire to maintain and operate for itself the system and enterprise herein authorized, the grantee shall surrender its franchise and will turn over to the Government all serviceable equipment therein, at fair market value, less reasonable depreciation."}},{"id":"PH-H3210-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Granting the Pioneer Electric and Ice Plant, Inc. a Franchise to Install, Operate and Maintain an Electric Light, Heat and Power System, and Ice Plant Service in the Municipality of Pagadian, Province of Zamboanga del Sur","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3211"] = {"id":"PH-H3211","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3908_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授予 Bautista Logging Company, Inc. 在菲律宾境内建设、维护和运营私人固定点对点与陆基无线电台的临时许可的法案","en":"An Act Granting the Bautista Logging Company, Inc. a Temporary Permit to Construct, Maintain and Operate Private Fixed Point-to-Point, Private Land-Based Radio Stations for the Reception and Transmission of Radio Communications Within the Philippines","orig":"An Act Granting the Bautista Logging Company, Inc. a Temporary Permit to Construct, Maintain and Operate Private Fixed Point-to-Point, Private Land-Based Radio Stations for the Reception and Transmission of Radio Communications Within the Philippines"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["general"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3908","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 13 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3908_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3211-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"Subject to the provisions of the Constitution and the provisions of Act Numbered Three thousand eight hundred and forty-six, entitled \"An Act providing for the regulation of radio stations and radio communications in the Philippine Islands, and for other purposes,\" Commonwealth Act Numbered One hundred forty-six, known as the Public Service Act, and their amendments, and other applicable laws, there is hereby granted to the Bautista Logging company, Inc., its successors or assigns, and hereunder referred to as the \"grantee,\" the right and privilege of constructing, installing, establishing and operating in the Philippines, at such places as its business may demand, subject to the approval of the Secretary of Public Works and Communications, private fixed point-to-point, and land-based radio stations for the reception and transmissions of wireless messages on radiotelephony, each station to consist of two radio apparatus comprising of a radio receiving and sending apparatus."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The President of the Philippines shall have the power and authority to permit the locations of said private fixed point-to-point and land-based radio stations or any of them on public domain upon such terms as he may prescribe."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This temporary permit shall continue to be in force during the time that the Government has not established similar service at the places selected by the grantee."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"The Bautista Logging Company, Inc., shall not engage in domestic business of telecommunications in the Philippines without further special assent of the Congress of the Philippines, it being understood that the purpose of this temporary permit is to secure to the grantee the right to construct, install, establish and operate private fixed point-to-point and land-based radio stations in places within the Philippines as its interest and that of its trade and business may justify."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"A special right is hereby reserved to the President of the Philippines in time of war, insurrection, public peril, emergency, calamity or disturbance of peace and order, to cause the closing of the station or stations of the grantee or to authorize the temporary use or possession thereof by any department of the Government upon payment of just compensation."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"No fees shall be charged by the grantee as the radio stations that may be established by virtue of this Act shall engage in communications regarding the grantee’s business only."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"The grantee, its successors or assigns, shall hold the national, provincial and municipal governments of the Philippines harmless from all claims, accounts, demands or actions arising out of accidents or injuries whether to property or to persons, caused by the construction or operation of the radio stations for reception and transmission of wireless messages by the grantee."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall so construct and operate its radio stations as not to interfere with the operation of other radio stations maintained and operated in the Philippines."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall be subject to the corporation laws of the Philippines now existing or which may hereafter be enacted."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"The grantee is hereby authorized to operate its private stations on commercial frequencies that may be assigned to it by the Radio Control Board."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall not lease, transfer, grant the usufruct of, sell or assign this temporary permit, nor the rights or privileges acquired thereunder to any person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity, nor merge with any other person, company, or corporation organized for the same purpose, without the approval of the Congress of the Philippines first had. Any corporation to which this temporary permit may be sold, transferred or assigned, shall be subject to the corporation laws of the Philippines now existing or hereafter enacted, and any person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity to which this temporary permit is sold, transferred, or assigned shall be subject to all conditions, terms, restrictions and limitations of this temporary permit as fully and completely and to the same extent as if the temporary permit had been originally granted to the said person, firm, company, corporation or other commercial or legal entity."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"This temporary permit shall be subject to amendment, alteration or repeal by the Congress of the Philippines when the public interest so requires, and shall not be interpreted mean as an exclusive grant of the privileges herein provided for."}},{"id":"PH-H3211-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Granting the Bautista Logging Company, Inc. a Temporary Permit to Construct, Maintain and Operate Private Fixed Point-to-Point, Private Land-Based Radio Stations for the Reception and Transmission of Radio Communications Within the Philippines","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3212"] = {"id":"PH-H3212","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3909_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授权萨马省Catbalogan市镇萨马工艺与贸易学校开设工业教育理学士（BSIE）与工业艺术理学士（BSIA）学位课程并授权为此拨款","en":"An Act Authoring the Samar School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Catbalogan, Province of Samar, to Offer Courses Leading to the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education (BSIE) and the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts (BSIA) and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds for the Purpose","orig":"An Act Authoring the Samar School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Catbalogan, Province of Samar, to Offer Courses Leading to the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education (BSIE) and the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts (BSIA) and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds for the Purpose"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education","culture"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3909","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3909_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3212-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The Samar School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Catbalogan, Province of Samar, is hereby authorized to offer courses leading to the degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education (BSIE) and the degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts (BSIA)."}},{"id":"PH-H3212-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"There is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, the sum of two hundred thousand pesos to carry into effect the provisions of this Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3212-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Authoring the Samar School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Catbalogan, Province of Samar, to Offer Courses Leading to the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education (BSIE) and the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts (BSIA) and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds for the Purpose","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3213"] = {"id":"PH-H3213","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3910_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授予Jose B. Jaucian在南甘马粦省Libmanan市镇电灯、热力与动力系统特许经营权的法案","en":"An Act Granting Jose B. Jaucian a Franchise for an Electric Light, Heat and Power System in the Municipality of Libmanan, Province of Camarines Sur","orig":"An Act Granting Jose B. Jaucian a Franchise for an Electric Light, Heat and Power System in the Municipality of Libmanan, Province of Camarines Sur"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["investment"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3910","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3910_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3213-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"Subject to the terms and conditions established in Act Numbered Thirty-six hundred thirty-six, as amended by Commonwealth Act Numbered One hundred thirty-two, and to the provisions of the Constitution, there is granted to Jose B. Jaucian, for a period of twenty-five years from the approval of this Act, the right, privilege and authority to construct, maintain and operate an electric light, heat and power system and/or obtain a power allocation from the National Power Corporation, for the purpose of generating and distributing electric light, heat and/or power for sale within the Municipality of Libmanan, Province of Camarines Sur."}},{"id":"PH-H3213-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"In the event that the grantee shall purchase and secure from the National Power Corporation electric heat and power, the National Power Corporation is hereby authorized to negotiate and transact for the benefit and in behalf of the public consumers with reference to rates."}},{"id":"PH-H3213-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"It is expressly provided that in the event the Government should desire to maintain and operate for itself the system and enterprise herein authorized, the grantee shall surrender its franchise and will turn over to the Government all serviceable equipment therein, at fair market value, less reasonable depreciation."}},{"id":"PH-H3213-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Granting Jose B. Jaucian a Franchise for an Electric Light, Heat and Power System in the Municipality of Libmanan, Province of Camarines Sur","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3214"] = {"id":"PH-H3214","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3911_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授权莱特区域工艺与贸易学校开设工业教育与工业艺术学士学位课程及夜班并为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act Authorizing the Leyte Regional School of Arts and Trades to Offer Teacher Education Curricula Leading to the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education and the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts, to Offer Evening Classes in Such Courses and in Trade and Industrial Education, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds for the Purpose","orig":"An Act Authorizing the Leyte Regional School of Arts and Trades to Offer Teacher Education Curricula Leading to the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education and the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts, to Offer Evening Classes in Such Courses and in Trade and Industrial Education, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds for the Purpose"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["trade","education","culture"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3911","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3911_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3214-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The Leyte Regional School of Arts and Trades situated in the City of Tacloban, is hereby authorized to offer teacher education curricula leading to the degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education and the degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts. Evening classes shall be offered in such courses and in trade and industrial education."}},{"id":"PH-H3214-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The sum of one hundred thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the operation and maintenance of the said curricula during the fiscal year nineteen hundred sixty-four to nineteen hundred sixty-five. Thereafter, the necessary funds for the purpose shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3214-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Authorizing the Leyte Regional School of Arts and Trades to Offer Teacher Education Curricula Leading to the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Education and the Degree of Bachelor of Science in Industrial Arts, to Offer Evening Classes in Such Courses and in Trade and Industrial Education, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds for the Purpose","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3215"] = {"id":"PH-H3215","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3912_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"延长原授予Natalio Digal、后售予Ocmis电力服务股份有限公司的电力特许权期限的法案","en":"An Act Extending the Term of the Electric Franchise Originally Granted to Natalio Digal but Subsequently Sold to Ocmis Electric Service Co., Inc.","orig":"An Act Extending the Term of the Electric Franchise Originally Granted to Natalio Digal but Subsequently Sold to Ocmis Electric Service Co., Inc."},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["investment"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3912","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3912_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3215-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The term of the franchise for an electric light, heat and power system granted to Natalio Digal under Act Numbered Thirty-six hundred forty-five, and subsequently sold and transferred to Ocmis Electric Service Co., Inc., by authority of Act Numbered Thirty-nine hundred fifty-one, is hereby extended with the same terms and conditions for a period of twenty-five years from December seven, nineteen hundred sixty-four."}},{"id":"PH-H3215-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Extending the Term of the Electric Franchise Originally Granted to Natalio Digal but Subsequently Sold to Ocmis Electric Service Co., Inc.","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3216"] = {"id":"PH-H3216","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3913_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"设立Tuguegarao市","en":"An Act Converting the Cagayan Valley School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Tuguegarao, Province of Cagayan, into a College and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act Converting the Cagayan Valley School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Tuguegarao, Province of Cagayan, into a College and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education","culture"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3913","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3913_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3216-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The Cagayan Valley School of Arts and Trades in the Municipality of Tuguegarao, Province of Cagayan, is hereby converted into a college to be known as Cagayan Valley School of Arts and Trades which shall be under the supervision of the Director of Vocational Education. The said college shall offer, in addition to its present curriculum, such collegiate courses as the said Director may determine."}},{"id":"PH-H3216-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The sum of one hundred fifty thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the conversion, operation and maintenance of said college during the fiscal year nineteen hundred and sixty-five. Such sums as may be necessary for its operation and maintenance in subsequent years shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3216-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45"};
  FT["PH-H3217"] = {"id":"PH-H3217","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3914_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将苏禄省帕蒂库尔市镇塔格利比中央小学的名称变更为Datu Uddin Bahjin中央小学的法案","en":"An Act Changing the Name of Taglibi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Patikul, Province of Sulu, to Datu Uddin Bahjin Central Elementary School","orig":"An Act Changing the Name of Taglibi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Patikul, Province of Sulu, to Datu Uddin Bahjin Central Elementary School"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3914","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3914_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3217-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The name of Taglibi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Patikul, Province of Sulu, is changed to Datu Uddin Bahjin Central Elementary School."}},{"id":"PH-H3217-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Changing the Name of Taglibi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Patikul, Province of Sulu, to Datu Uddin Bahjin Central Elementary School","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3218"] = {"id":"PH-H3218","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3915_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将苏禄省卢克市镇卡伦东小学的名称变更为Hadji Maharaja Tawasil小学的法案","en":"An Act Changing the Name of Karundong Elementary School in the Municipality of Luuk, Province of Sulu, to Hadji Maharaja Tawasil Elementary School","orig":"An Act Changing the Name of Karundong Elementary School in the Municipality of Luuk, Province of Sulu, to Hadji Maharaja Tawasil Elementary School"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3915","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3915_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3218-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The name of Karundong Elementary School in the Municipality of Luuk, Province of Sulu, is changed to Hadji Maharaja Tawasil Elementary School."}},{"id":"PH-H3218-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Changing the Name of Karundong Elementary School in the Municipality of Luuk, Province of Sulu, to Hadji Maharaja Tawasil Elementary School","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3219"] = {"id":"PH-H3219","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3916_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"设立Altavas市","en":"An Act Converting Altavas High School in the Municipality of Altavas, Province of Aklan, into a National School to be Known as Altavas National School, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act Converting Altavas High School in the Municipality of Altavas, Province of Aklan, into a National School to be Known as Altavas National School, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3916","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3916_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3219-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The Altavas High School in the Municipality of Altavas, Province of Aklan, is hereby converted into a national school to be known as Altavas National School, General as well as vocational courses shall be offered in said school."}},{"id":"PH-H3219-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Secretary of Education is hereby empowered to reorganize said school accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H3219-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The sum of two hundred thousand pesos, or so much thereof as may be necessary, is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, to carry out the purpose of this Act during the fiscal year nineteen hundred sixty-five. Thereafter, such sums as may be needed for its operation shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3219-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45"};
  FT["PH-H3220"] = {"id":"PH-H3220","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3917_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":17,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"设立Indang市","en":"An Act Converting the Don Severino National Agricultural School in the Municipality of Indang, Province of Cavite, into a College, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act Converting the Don Severino National Agricultural School in the Municipality of Indang, Province of Cavite, into a College, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education","environment"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3917","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 17 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3917_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3220-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The Don Severino National Agricultural School in the Municipality of Indang, Province of Cavite, is hereby converted into a college, to be known as Don Severino Agricultural College which shall offer not only its present four-year secondary agricultural course and special courses, but also a two-year course leading to the title of Associate in Agricultural Education; four-year course leading to the degrees of Bachelor of Science in Agriculture, Bachelor of Science in Agricultural Education, Bachelor of Science in Home Technology, and Bachelor of Science in Agricultural Engineering; post graduate course leading to the degrees of Master of Science in Agriculture Master of Science in Agricultural Education and Master of Science in Home Technology; and other degree courses and special courses as the board of trustees of the college may deem necessary."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The aim of the said college shall be to provide professional, technical and special instruction for special purposes and to promote research, extension services and progressive leadership in agriculture, agricultural education, home technology and other educational fields."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The head of this institution shall be known as the President of the Don Severino Agricultural College. He shall be appointed by the President of the Philippines upon the recommendation of the board of trustees as hereinafter provided. The powers and duties of the president of the college, in addition to those specially provided for in this Act, shall be those usually pertaining to the office of the president of a college."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"The government of said college is hereby vested in a board of trustees of the Don Severino Agricultural College. The board of trustees shall be composed of the Secretary of Education, who shall be ex-officio chairman of the board, the chairman of the Committee on Education of the Senate, the chairman of the Committee on Education of the House of Representatives, the Director of Public Schools, the president of the college and the president of the Don Severino Agricultural College Alumni Association.\nMembers of the board shall serve without compensation, other than actual and necessary expenses incurred either in attendance upon meetings of the board or upon other official business authorized by resolution of the board."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"The board of trustees shall have the following powers and duties, in addition to its general powers of administration:\n(a) To receive and appropriate to the ends specified by law such sums of money as may be provided by law for the support of the college;\n(b) To confer the title of Associate in Agricultural Education, the degrees of Bachelor of Science in Agriculture, Bachelor of Science in Agricultural Engineering, Bachelor of Science in Home Technology, and such other titles and degrees corresponding to the courses which the board of trustees may offer: Provided, That it may confer the usual honorary degrees upon any person in recognition of learning, statemanship, leadership or eminence in literature, science, art, agriculture or public service;\n(c) To appoint, upon the recommendation of the president of the college, instructors, professors, lecturers and other employees of the college; to fix their compensation, hours of service and such other duties and conditions as may be deemed proper; to grant to them in its discretion leaves of absence under such regulations as it may promulgate, any provision of law to the contrary notwithstanding, and to remove them for cause after an investigation and hearing shall have been conducted;\n(d) To approve the curricula and rules of discipline drawn up by the college council as hereinafter provided;\n(e) To fix the tuition fees required of students, as well as matriculation fees, graduation fees and fees for laboratory courses and all special fees, and to remit the same in special cases;\n(f) To provide fellowship for faculty members and scholarships to students showing special evidence of merit;\n(g) To provide rules for its own government, and to enact, for the government of the college, such general ordinances and regulations not contrary to law, as are consistent with the purposes of the college, as defined in Section two of this Act; and\n(h) To receive in trust legacies, gifts, donations of real and personal property of all kinds and to administer the same for the benefit of the college or for aid to any student, in accordance with the directions and instructions of the donor, and in default therefor, in such manner as the board of trustees may, in its discretion, determine."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"A quorum of the board of trustees shall consist of a majority of all the members. All processes against the board of trustees shall be served on the president or secretary thereof."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"On or before the fifteenth of June of each year, the board of trustees shall file with the President of the Philippines a detailed report, setting forth the progress, condition and needs of the college."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"There shall be a college council consisting of the president of the college as presiding officer and of all instructors and professors of the college as members. The council shall have the power to prescribe the curricula and rules of discipline of the college, subject to the approval of the board of trustees. It shall fix the requirements for admission to the college, as well as for graduation and the award of a title or a degree. The council shall also have the power to recommend students or other persons to be awarded titles or degree. Through the president, it shall have disciplinary power over the students within the limits prescribed by the rules and discipline approved by the board of trustees."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"The body of the instructors and professors of the college shall constitute the faculty of the college. In the appointment of professors or instructors of the college, no religious test shall be applied nor shall religious opinions or affiliations of any of the faculty members be made a matter of examination or inquiry: Provided, However, That no instructor or professor in the college shall inculcate sectarian tenets in any of his teachings, nor shall he attempt either directly or indirectly, under penalty of dismissal, to influence for or against any particular church or religious sect."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"No civil service eligibility shall be required for appointment to the college as a professor or regular instructor."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"There shall be a secretary of the college, appointed by the board of trustees, who shall also act as the secretary of the board, and who shall keep such records of the college as may be designated by the board."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"The Treasurer of the Philippines shall be ex-officio treasurer of the college, and all accounts and expenses thereof shall be audited by the Auditor General or his duly authorized representatives, and all disbursements shall be made in accordance with rules and regulations prescribed by him."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"Heads of bureaus or offices of the national government are hereby authorized to loan or transfer, upon request of the president of the college, such apparatus or supplies as may be needed by the college, and to detail employees for duty therein, when, in the judgment of the head of bureau or office, such supplies or employees can be spared without serious detriment to the public service. Employees so detailed shall perform such duties as may be required of them by the head of the institution, and the time they spend under detail shall be counted as part of their regular official service."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"text":{"en":"The president of the college, with the approval of the Director of Public Schools, may use one or more public schools as training or laboratory schools of the college."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"text":{"en":"In order not to interrupt the smooth functioning of the four-year secondary agricultural curriculum of the Don Severino National Agricultural School, the faculty of the school, consisting of the principal and teachers, as well as the other personnel, shall be absorbed by the new college. Salaries of the personnel, shall be adjusted in the discretion of the board of trustees within the amount available for appropriation, and all properties, assets and equipment of the school, as well as all its liabilities, shall be absorbed by the college."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"text":{"en":"For the purpose of giving effect to this Act, all the unexpended balance of appropriation under the control of the former Don Severino National Agricultural School are hereby made available for the operation of the Don Severino Agricultural College until June thirty nineteen hundred sixty-four. Thereafter, the sum of five hundred thousand pesos or so much thereof as may be needed shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act for the use of the college. It will cover the salaries of the president and the personnel of the college and shall be used for such other expenses as may be necessary to implement the provisions of this Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3220-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45"};
  FT["PH-H3221"] = {"id":"PH-H3221","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3918_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将苏禄省 Panamao市镇 Seit 中央小学的名称变更为Panglima Agga 中央小学的法案","en":"An Act Changing the Name of the Seit Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Panamao, Province of Sulu, to Panglima Agga Central Elementary School","orig":"An Act Changing the Name of the Seit Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Panamao, Province of Sulu, to Panglima Agga Central Elementary School"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3918","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3918_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3221-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The name of the Seit Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Panamao, Province of Sulu, is changed to Panglima Agga Central Elementary School."}},{"id":"PH-H3221-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Changing the Name of the Seit Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Panamao, Province of Sulu, to Panglima Agga Central Elementary School","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3222"] = {"id":"PH-H3222","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3919_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将苏禄省西亚西市镇西亚西中央小学的名称变更为Panglima Julkanain Taup小学的法案","en":"An Act Changing the Name of the Siasi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Siasi, Province of Sulu, to Panglima Julkanain Taup Elementary School","orig":"An Act Changing the Name of the Siasi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Siasi, Province of Sulu, to Panglima Julkanain Taup Elementary School"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3919","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3919_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3222-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The name of Siasi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Siasi, Province of Sulu, is hereby to Panglima Julkanain Taup Elementary School."}},{"id":"PH-H3222-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Changing the Name of the Siasi Central Elementary School in the Municipality of Siasi, Province of Sulu, to Panglima Julkanain Taup Elementary School","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3223"] = {"id":"PH-H3223","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3920_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"授予 Dr. Leoncio Opulencia 在拉古纳省 Los Baños 市镇建设、运营制冰厂与冷藏库并在该省及 San Pablo 市销售冰和供应冷藏的特许权法案","en":"An Act Granting Dr. Leoncio Opulencia a Franchise to Construct, Operate and Maintain an Ice Plant and Cold Storage in the Municipality of Los Baños, Province of Laguna, and to Sell Ice and Supply Cold Storage Within the Province of Laguna and the City of San Pablo","orig":"An Act Granting Dr. Leoncio Opulencia a Franchise to Construct, Operate and Maintain an Ice Plant and Cold Storage in the Municipality of Los Baños, Province of Laguna, and to Sell Ice and Supply Cold Storage Within the Province of Laguna and the City of San Pablo"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["investment"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3920","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 8 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3920_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3223-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"Subject to the conditions imposed by this Act, there is hereby granted to Dr. Leoncio Opulencia, hereinafter referred to as the grantee, a franchise to construct, operate and maintain an ice plant and cold storage in the Municipality of Los Baños, Province of Laguna, for the purpose of manufacturing and distributing ice and supplying cold storage within the Province of Laguna and the City of San Pablo, and to charge and collect a schedule of prices and rates for the ice and cold storage so furnished, which schedule of prices and rates shall at all times be subject to regulation by the Public Service Commission."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The grantee shall manufacture and supply ice up to the limit of the capacity of his plant."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"All the apparatus and appurtenances to be used by the grantee shall be modern, safe and first class in every respect, and the grantee shall, whenever the Public Service Commission shall determine that public interest reasonably requires it, change or alter any of the apparatus and appurtenances at grantee's expense."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This franchise shall continue for a period of twenty-five years from the date the said plant and cold storage shall be placed in operation and/or shall commence the manufacture and distribution of ice in the Province of Laguna and the City of San Pablo, and is made subject to the express condition that the same shall be null and void unless the construction of said plant and cold storage be begun within four years from the date of the approval of this Act and completed within six years from said date, except when prevented by an act of God, or force majeure, martial law, riot, civil commotion, usurpation by military power or any other cause beyond the grantee's control."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"The books, records and accounts of the grantee shall always be open to the inspection of the provincial treasurer or his authorized representatives, and it shall be the duty of the grantee to submit to the provincial treasurer quarterly reports in duplicate, showing the gross receipts for the quarter past, one which shall be forwarded by the provincial treasurer to the Auditor General, who shall keep the same on file."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"This franchise is granted subject to the provisions of Commonwealth Act Numbered One hundred forty-six, as amended, only with respect to the fixing of rates and with the understanding and upon the condition that it shall be subject to amendment, alteration or repeal by the Congress of the Philippines when public interest so requires."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"In the event of any competing individual, association of persons or corporation receiving from the Congress of the Philippines a similar franchise in which there shall be any term or terms more favorable than those herein granted or tending to place the herein grantee at any disadvantage, then such term or terms shall ipso facto become a part of the terms hereof and shall operate equally in favor of the grantee as in the case of said competing individual, association of persons, or corporation."}},{"id":"PH-H3223-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964"}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Granting Dr. Leoncio Opulencia a Franchise to Construct, Operate and Maintain an Ice Plant and Cold Storage in the Municipality of Los Baños, Province of Laguna, and to Sell Ice and Supply Cold Storage Within the Province of Laguna and the City of San Pablo","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3224"] = {"id":"PH-H3224","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3921_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将卡皮斯省罗哈斯总统市镇蒂嫩丹小学的名称变更为Elizalde纪念小学的法案","en":"An Act Changing the Name of Tinundan Elementary School in the Municipality of President Roxas, Province of Capiz, to Elizalde Memorial Elementary School","orig":"An Act Changing the Name of Tinundan Elementary School in the Municipality of President Roxas, Province of Capiz, to Elizalde Memorial Elementary School"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3921","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3921_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3224-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The name of Tinundan Elementary School in the Municipality of President Roxas, Province of Capiz, is hereby changed to Elizalde Memorial Elementary School."}},{"id":"PH-H3224-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Changing the Name of Tinundan Elementary School in the Municipality of President Roxas, Province of Capiz, to Elizalde Memorial Elementary School","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3225"] = {"id":"PH-H3225","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3922_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"在伊莎贝拉省Santiago市镇设立职业与工业中学并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of a Vocational and Industrial High School in the Municipality of Santiago, Province of Isabela, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of a Vocational and Industrial High School in the Municipality of Santiago, Province of Isabela, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3922","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3922_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3225-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There shall be established under the supervision of the Director of Vocational Education, a vocational and industrial high school in the Municipality of Santiago, Province of Isabela, to be known as Santiago Vocational and Industrial High School."}},{"id":"PH-H3225-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Director of Vocational Education shall issue such rules and regulations as may be necessary to carry out the purpose of the Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3225-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The sum of one hundred and fifty thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the establishment, operation and maintenance of said school during the fiscal year nineteen hundred and sixty-five. Thereafter, the necessary funds needed for its operation and maintenance shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3225-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of a Vocational and Industrial High School in the Municipality of Santiago, Province of Isabela, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3226"] = {"id":"PH-H3226","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3923_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"将哥打巴托省 Nuling市镇 Mapoti 小学的名称变更为Nibuaya 小学的法案","en":"An Act Changing the Name of Mapoti Primary School in the Municipality of Nuling, Province of Cotabato, to Nibuaya Primary School","orig":"An Act Changing the Name of Mapoti Primary School in the Municipality of Nuling, Province of Cotabato, to Nibuaya Primary School"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["education"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3923","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3923_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3226-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"The name of Mapoti Primary School in the Municipality of Nuling, Province of Cotabato, is hereby changed to Nibuaya Primary School."}},{"id":"PH-H3226-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Changing the Name of Mapoti Primary School in the Municipality of Nuling, Province of Cotabato, to Nibuaya Primary School","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["PH-H3227"] = {"id":"PH-H3227","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation）","sourceUrl":"https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3924_1964.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-06","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"在伊莎贝拉省Cauayan市镇设立急诊医院，名称为Cauayan伊莎贝拉急诊医院，并授权为此拨款的法案","en":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of an Emergency Hospital in the Municipality of Cauayan, Province of Isabela, to be Known as Cauayan Isabela Emergency Hospital, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","orig":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of an Emergency Hospital in the Municipality of Cauayan, Province of Isabela, to be Known as Cauayan Isabela Emergency Hospital, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor"},"level":"law","status":"active","topics":["health"],"docNumber":"Republic Act No. 3924","issuingBody":"Congress of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1964-06-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil 菲律宾法律虚拟图书馆（The LawPhil Project – Arellano Law Foundation） 官方页面（statutes/repacts/ra1964/ra_3924_1964.html），未改写、未摘译、未节选；原文语言：英语。 条文抬头依源文为 “Section N.” 等形式，本库统一规范为 “Section N.”；首行抬头与条内标题的分段依源文块级边界还原。","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H3227-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"There shall be established under the direct supervision of the Director of Medical Services, an emergency hospital in the Municipality of Cauayan, Province of Isabela, to be known as Cauayan Emergency Hospital. The site for the said hospital shall be provided by the municipal council of the Municipality of Cauayan, in consultation with the Director of Medical Services."}},{"id":"PH-H3227-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Secretary of Health shall promulgate such rules and regulations as may be necessary to carry into effect the purpose of this Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3227-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The sum of two hundred thousand pesos is hereby authorized to be appropriated out of any funds in the National Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the establishment, operation and maintenance of said hospital during the fiscal year nineteen hundred sixty-five. Such sum as may be necessary for its operation and maintenance in subsequent years shall be included in the annual General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H3227-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"This Act shall take effect upon its approval.\nApproved: June 18, 1964."}}],"pack":"ph-p45","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1837-PH-7575","source":"An Act Providing for the Establishment of an Emergency Hospital in the Municipality of Cauayan, Province of Isabela, to be Known as Cauayan Isabela Emergency Hospital, and Authorizing the Appropriation of Funds Therefor","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
